From 45b4c98f8b1ba252b2846a9dc742f9a54852728b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:42:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] fix(controlplane): serialize stores that share a SQLite
 connection

TaskStore and Outbox each managed a bare sqlite3 connection without a
lock, and the only way to put an Outbox write into a business
transaction was to hand it someone else's connection. sqlite3
transactions belong to the connection, so interleaving threads let one
side's commit or rollback take the other side's uncommitted writes with
it (the hazard already fixed inside the registry for R-1).

Introduce controlplane.sqlite.Database: one connection plus a
re-entrant lock. call()/run() roll back whatever the function left
uncommitted when it raises and refuse to leave a transaction open;
transaction() is a BEGIN IMMEDIATE unit of work. The registry,
TaskStore and Outbox now go through it. TaskStore and Outbox accept
database= to share one connection, and Outbox.database replaces the raw
conn property and conn= argument.

This also fixes the registry leaving a partial write behind when a
write path raised anything other than IntegrityError: the next commit
on the connection used to commit it.
